### Three claims I passed to agents that were WRONG

Recorded because in each case the agent measured rather than trusting me, and
that is the behaviour to keep asking for:

1. **`net-kotobase` has vendored copies in more than one source tree** -- it does
   not; the second-tree hits were shadow-cljs analysis cache.
2. **`worker/` was renamed to `clj-edge/`, 48 files, 100% similarity** -- it went
   to `kotobase-edge/`, 57 files, and neither rename was uniformly R100. This one
   originated in a commit message I wrote from an earlier agent's report, then
   propagated into a brief. See the section above on how it travelled.
3. **The `TODO_EXIT_NODE_IP` placeholder fails closed because of the
   underscore** -- it does not. Measured three ways: httpx accepts and lowercases
   it, `getaddrinfo` resolves underscore labels, and an end-to-end run against a
   stub listener delivered the trust header and the peer key. What actually stops
   it is that nothing answers for a DOTLESS name on the current search path,
   which is environmental, not structural -- and a dotless name is exactly what a
   search suffix completes (k8s uses `ndots:5`).

Finding 3 also overturned the fix's premise: a ConfigMap in another repo ships
the placeholder **verbatim as the value**, so `unset` was never the risk and a
require-non-empty check would have passed on the only deployment that exists.
The landed fix rejects the placeholder by name.

